WEBVTT

01:33.218 --> 01:36.679
The first time I felt another person
direct their intent to kill at me

01:37.514 --> 01:41.309
was shortly before my parents
left the village.

01:42.560 --> 01:44.270
He was probably a bandit.

01:44.854 --> 01:46.940
I was deep in the mountains
hunting with Father...

01:47.690 --> 01:50.401
when I was nearly killed.

01:51.736 --> 01:55.031
"You are not needed in this world."

01:55.824 --> 01:57.325
That aura of powerful denial.

02:00.703 --> 02:04.040
I felt it penetrating
every pore of my body,

02:04.874 --> 02:10.421
piercing my skin
and stabbing directly into my flesh.

02:26.062 --> 02:27.147
Yuru!

02:28.523 --> 02:29.399
Yuru!

02:30.400 --> 02:32.777
Are you all right? Are you hurt?

02:34.279 --> 02:37.365
This is... his blood.

02:37.448 --> 02:38.992
I'm sorry.

02:39.742 --> 02:41.452
I shouldn't have taken my eyes off you.

02:43.371 --> 02:46.082
What... What is this?

02:47.458 --> 02:49.836
Yuru, remember this.

02:50.503 --> 02:52.171
This is the intent to kill.

02:55.675 --> 02:58.511
You'll probably experience it again
in the future. No...

02:59.470 --> 03:03.516
As long as you're alive, it will probably
be thrown at you countless times.

03:04.225 --> 03:08.605
Do not hesitate against
those who direct it at you.

03:31.127 --> 03:33.630
Have you calmed down some, Yuru?

03:35.590 --> 03:39.636
We'll head back to the village
after spending the night on the mountain.

03:39.719 --> 03:41.888
You can take your time calming down.

03:41.971 --> 03:47.018
Breathe in deeply and let it out slowly.

03:49.020 --> 03:49.854
That's it.

03:49.938 --> 03:53.900
Let your anxiety out with your breath.

03:54.734 --> 03:58.571
There are moments when fear can kill you.

03:59.072 --> 04:04.410
Especially for hunters like us,
who fight for our lives against beasts.

04:05.662 --> 04:10.458
Calm down, analyze the situation,
and determine what you should do.

04:10.541 --> 04:15.630
Always consider how you can use
the materials at hand to survive.

04:17.840 --> 04:22.095
Death strikes where
fear makes us vulnerable.

04:26.849 --> 04:28.017
Listen, Yuru.

04:28.685 --> 04:31.562
Don't tell the villagers you
were attacked by a bandit.

04:32.146 --> 04:36.693
Why not? The bandit's allies
could attack the village.

04:36.776 --> 04:39.362
We have to tell the others.

04:39.445 --> 04:42.198
No, they won't attack our village.

04:43.783 --> 04:45.159
Don't tell anyone.

04:45.243 --> 04:48.454
When we get back to the village,
act like you always do.

04:49.038 --> 04:51.332
As though nothing happened.

04:52.917 --> 04:54.460
Remain calm.

05:03.386 --> 05:04.679
Mine-san!

05:05.722 --> 05:07.015
We're back.

05:07.098 --> 05:08.641
We're glad you're back.

05:08.725 --> 05:12.687
We were worried when we heard you
didn't come back last night.

05:12.770 --> 05:14.022
Sorry about that.

05:14.105 --> 05:16.816
We chased our quarry deep
into the mountains.

05:17.483 --> 05:19.610
Since I had Yuru with me,
we played it safe

05:19.694 --> 05:21.446
and spent the night out there.

05:22.030 --> 05:24.907
You camped out overnight
and have nothing to show for it?

05:24.991 --> 05:27.035
That's unusual for you.

05:29.037 --> 05:30.330
It happens.

05:33.499 --> 05:34.334
Mine-san!

05:36.419 --> 05:38.838
We're back, Kyoka-san.

05:38.921 --> 05:41.924
Good. Yuru's with you.

05:42.008 --> 05:45.219
We were worried when you didn't come back.

05:47.180 --> 05:49.724
Did something happen in the mountains?

05:50.683 --> 05:52.143
No, nothing.

05:52.226 --> 05:53.978
We just chased our quarry too far.

05:59.734 --> 06:01.611
Did you get hurt?

06:04.989 --> 06:06.824
It's the blood of the rat
we ate for dinner.

06:07.408 --> 06:09.077
Boy, am I hungry.

06:09.160 --> 06:11.454
That rat wasn't nearly enough food.

06:12.205 --> 06:14.248
Where's Nagisa? With Asa?

06:14.332 --> 06:17.085
- Yes, she's inside.
- Okay.

06:17.168 --> 06:20.046
Let's have breakfast together, Yuru.

06:20.129 --> 06:20.963
Okay.

06:23.341 --> 06:24.383
Nagisa.

06:25.968 --> 06:27.303
We're back, Mother.

06:27.970 --> 06:29.597
Welcome home.

06:29.680 --> 06:31.390
I was so worried when you didn't return.

06:31.474 --> 06:32.308
Sorry.

06:33.101 --> 06:34.519
Sorry, Asa.

06:34.602 --> 06:37.897
We went deep into the mountains
and were late coming back.

06:37.980 --> 06:39.232
Were you hurt?

06:39.816 --> 06:41.234
Are you okay, Brother?

06:41.317 --> 06:43.820
Nothing happened. I'm totally fine.

06:44.529 --> 06:45.530
Nothing happened.

06:46.614 --> 06:51.410
Man... I was too anxious to sleep
while camping out.

06:51.494 --> 06:53.704
I'm a little tired.

06:54.664 --> 06:55.498
Brother.

06:56.833 --> 06:59.127
Take care of yourself.

07:09.595 --> 07:12.390
I almost had it.

07:12.974 --> 07:14.517
- It was really big.
- Nagisa.

07:14.600 --> 07:17.353
I'm sure you'll get it next time.

07:18.354 --> 07:21.899
- Yeah.
- Yeah. I'm looking forward to it.

07:30.867 --> 07:32.952
Shortly after that,

07:33.578 --> 07:37.665
Father and Mother left the village
without me and Asa.

07:38.166 --> 07:39.834
Or so I thought.

07:40.334 --> 07:42.962
I was actually the only one left behind.

07:43.671 --> 07:47.967
Father and Mother
fled the village with Asa.

07:48.676 --> 07:51.179
The girl I thought was my sister

07:51.262 --> 07:54.974
whom I lived with for ten years
was an impostor.

07:56.434 --> 07:57.602
For ten years,

07:57.685 --> 08:00.688
the people of Higashi Village lied to me.

08:01.898 --> 08:05.651
Or so the self-proclaimed "real" Asa said.

08:06.360 --> 08:08.946
According to her...

08:10.031 --> 08:13.117
I died once.

08:14.494 --> 08:16.537
I was killed
by a Higashi Village assassin.

08:24.337 --> 08:28.341
We fled Higashi Village
and evaded our pursuers.

08:28.841 --> 08:31.177
Then the Kagemori clan took us in.

08:31.260 --> 08:34.138
We thought things had calmed down,

08:34.222 --> 08:36.933
but then Father and Mother went missing.

08:37.016 --> 08:41.145
Last year, when I was fifteen,
I was captured by an assassin.

08:41.229 --> 08:46.526
I was killed then
and gained the power of Break.

08:55.952 --> 08:58.579
This is the power of the Daemon

08:58.663 --> 09:02.375
that lives on the boundary
between the land of the dead and ours.

09:08.798 --> 09:12.552
The Daemon I met had the power of Break.

09:15.638 --> 09:18.558
Oh? Some flesh has arrived.

09:20.601 --> 09:21.644
Huh?

09:24.188 --> 09:27.066
I was cut
by a Higashi Village assassin, and...

09:27.149 --> 09:28.276
You died.

09:30.152 --> 09:33.698
You died once.

09:34.949 --> 09:36.742
Then is this hell?

09:37.243 --> 09:41.122
I suppose this place doesn't
look like paradise.

09:41.205 --> 09:42.039
Wait.

09:42.123 --> 09:48.629
Why do you assume you'd be sent
straight to hell upon your death?

09:49.380 --> 09:52.466
What kind of life did
you live in your world?

09:55.303 --> 10:00.474
This is the boundary between
the land of the dead and your world.

10:04.145 --> 10:07.523
Let's see... Where is it?

10:13.529 --> 10:15.573
Here. This is it.

10:16.741 --> 10:21.704
In your country, this place
is known as Yomotsu Hirasaka.

10:24.165 --> 10:26.626
It's just like Father said.

10:27.126 --> 10:29.086
According to the village legend,

10:29.170 --> 10:30.212
"Male and female twins

10:30.296 --> 10:32.340
born in the eastern village
before and after daybreak

10:32.423 --> 10:35.509
on a day when the day and night
are equal lengths

10:35.593 --> 10:39.305
will travel to the shadow realm
to command Daemons."

10:39.972 --> 10:43.559
Oral traditions always
get distorted over time.

10:43.643 --> 10:47.063
To be precise, it's "just
before the shadow realm."

10:48.272 --> 10:53.110
The people of Higashi Village
actually tried to kill me.

10:53.861 --> 10:57.031
Well, you can't come here unless you die.

10:57.782 --> 11:00.743
- So, what will you do now?
- What?

11:01.535 --> 11:05.081
Humans who come here have
two paths to choose from.

11:05.790 --> 11:09.168
Remain dead or accept me.

11:09.835 --> 11:13.506
If you wish to die,
simply fall from that path.

11:14.298 --> 11:16.801
If you want to live,

11:16.884 --> 11:20.805
accept me, the power of Break,
and return to the world of the living.

11:21.806 --> 11:23.557
It's convenient.

11:23.641 --> 11:25.518
As long as you can see him,

11:25.601 --> 11:29.897
you can "break" the enemy commander's head
off his body on the battlefield.

11:29.980 --> 11:33.567
You can end wars by yourself.

11:34.151 --> 11:37.530
Depending on the era,
you could become a hero.

11:38.030 --> 11:40.783
There are plenty
of other ways to use it, too.

11:41.575 --> 11:46.038
But in exchange, those who wish
to use you will gather around you.

11:46.705 --> 11:49.708
You may experience a living hell.

11:49.792 --> 11:54.213
You may think you're better off dead.

11:54.713 --> 11:57.508
My personal hell may have already begun.

11:58.717 --> 12:00.928
Father and Mother were kidnapped.

12:01.011 --> 12:03.055
I don't know what happened to them.

12:03.931 --> 12:07.935
Because I was born, they...

12:09.937 --> 12:13.274
Wait! Has my brother already come here?

12:13.858 --> 12:15.025
Has he been killed?

12:15.693 --> 12:17.278
I don't know.

12:17.361 --> 12:21.240
When he dies, he'll go to where Seal is.

12:21.740 --> 12:23.701
He hasn't been here.

12:25.077 --> 12:29.206
I don't know what's happened
to your brother.

12:35.421 --> 12:37.339
I can't die.

12:38.382 --> 12:40.926
We left my brother behind in the village.

12:41.427 --> 12:43.471
I don't know if he's still alive.

12:44.054 --> 12:46.307
Maybe he's been killed, like me.

12:46.807 --> 12:48.726
I have to go save him.

12:49.351 --> 12:51.520
I can't die yet!

12:52.313 --> 12:55.941
Choose. Life or death.

13:03.282 --> 13:05.910
You have beautiful eyes.

13:06.410 --> 13:08.245
Only look forward as you advance.

13:08.329 --> 13:10.122
Don't turn back.

13:21.425 --> 13:23.969
Hey, she's not coming back to life!

13:24.053 --> 13:25.638
But...

13:25.721 --> 13:27.389
They're the first twins in 400 years!

13:27.473 --> 13:29.058
They were finally born!

13:29.141 --> 13:32.561
Maybe she's a decoy prepared
by the Kagemori clan.

13:32.645 --> 13:34.563
I saw this girl in the village.

13:34.647 --> 13:35.606
I'm sure it's her.

13:36.273 --> 13:39.443
Yeah, years ago, when she was a kid.

13:39.527 --> 13:41.862
In a gloomy cell, no less.

13:41.946 --> 13:44.281
You couldn't have seen her face clearly.

13:44.365 --> 13:46.075
I know it's her.

13:46.158 --> 13:48.118
Then we failed to resurrect her.

13:48.202 --> 13:50.412
We can't get the power of Break anymore.

13:50.496 --> 13:52.498
There's still Seal.

13:52.581 --> 13:55.918
Seal is more than strong enough
to control the underworld.

13:56.001 --> 14:00.965
The brother's completely brainwashed
by the village, so he'll obey us.

14:01.048 --> 14:02.800
We should kill him and...

14:23.445 --> 14:24.530
Did you find Asa?

14:25.573 --> 14:26.532
Where?

14:28.242 --> 14:29.535
Asa!

14:30.661 --> 14:31.954
Asa!

14:41.547 --> 14:43.299
Asa, you dummy.

14:44.842 --> 14:49.555
You should leave the killing
to misfits like us.

14:50.431 --> 14:52.016
Sorry, Gabby-chan.

14:52.558 --> 14:56.770
I didn't choose to be a chosen twin,

14:57.271 --> 14:59.899
but now, I'm following the path I chose.

15:01.567 --> 15:03.527
I'll get my own hands dirty.

15:07.281 --> 15:09.241
I'm sorry, Brother.

15:09.950 --> 15:14.997
The perfect, little, adorable,
and innocent Asa you knew

15:15.915 --> 15:19.627
is gone now.

15:28.886 --> 15:31.096
They were an ox and horse?

15:31.680 --> 15:33.849
Like Ox-Head and Horse-Face, I guess?

15:33.933 --> 15:36.602
They're old but well-maintained.

15:37.311 --> 15:39.730
They must've been well-loved.

15:49.406 --> 15:51.700
Man, I'm hungry.

15:52.201 --> 15:53.869
I wonder what's for breakfast.

16:02.169 --> 16:04.380
Good morning.

16:04.922 --> 16:06.799
Is anybody home?

16:07.383 --> 16:10.636
Good morning, Kagemori clan.

16:10.719 --> 16:13.389
Huh? Should I push this call button?

16:13.973 --> 16:16.558
Don't rich people have guards
watching the gate?

16:18.060 --> 16:18.894
Who are you?

16:20.187 --> 16:21.021
There you are.

16:22.106 --> 16:24.358
Hello, Kagemori clan.

16:24.441 --> 16:27.027
Sorry, I know it's early.

16:27.111 --> 16:28.904
The name's Tadera Ryu.

16:29.571 --> 16:31.991
I'm here to pick up Yuru.

16:33.283 --> 16:34.410
Someone from the Tadera clan?

16:35.244 --> 16:36.286
Dera-san?

16:37.037 --> 16:39.164
Apparently, he's here for Mr. Big Brother.

16:39.248 --> 16:41.917
I'd completely forgotten about Dera.

16:42.001 --> 16:43.669
What shall we do?

16:43.752 --> 16:45.129
Oh, right.

16:45.629 --> 16:47.673
We didn't tell him when we left.

16:48.632 --> 16:50.426
I trust the Kagemori clan.

16:50.509 --> 16:52.302
They're a pain in the ass.

16:52.386 --> 16:55.556
Honestly, I'd rather not
get involved with them.

16:56.849 --> 17:01.103
It'd be best to hear out
both sides at the same time.

17:03.022 --> 17:06.400
Could you have Dera-san come here?

17:06.483 --> 17:08.193
Very well.

17:08.277 --> 17:10.279
Akio, bring him to the entrance.

17:10.863 --> 17:11.864
Yes, sir.

17:11.947 --> 17:13.907
Don't kill anyone this time.

17:13.991 --> 17:16.535
I won't. I said I was sorry.

17:19.079 --> 17:20.873
Good morning, Jin.

17:22.041 --> 17:23.917
The mansion is quite a mess.

17:24.001 --> 17:25.335
Did something happen?

17:25.419 --> 17:28.464
Good morning, Asuma-san.

17:28.547 --> 17:31.592
A number of external Daemon Wielders
entered the mansion

17:31.675 --> 17:33.218
and went on a rampage.

17:33.302 --> 17:35.345
Well, that must've been difficult.

17:35.929 --> 17:39.016
And yet, you didn't come to help
despite the disturbance.

17:39.099 --> 17:40.476
What were you up to?

17:40.559 --> 17:41.977
Sleeping.

17:42.978 --> 17:46.482
You didn't hear the commotion
even with your keen hearing?

17:47.066 --> 17:49.443
Whoa, what is all this?

17:49.526 --> 17:51.403
What is this, Jin-kun?

17:51.487 --> 17:53.489
Good morning, Hagure-kun.

17:53.572 --> 17:55.866
Good morning, Asuma-kun.

17:55.949 --> 17:57.618
What happened here?

17:57.701 --> 17:59.369
Was there an earthquake?

17:59.453 --> 18:04.333
A number of external Daemon Wielders
targeting the twins attacked the mansion.

18:04.416 --> 18:06.502
What? Is Asa-chan okay?

18:06.585 --> 18:09.379
Sorry for the disturbance. I'm fine.

18:09.463 --> 18:11.757
Oh, good.

18:12.257 --> 18:15.385
Wait, twins? You mean...

18:15.886 --> 18:17.638
Her brother is here, too.

18:18.305 --> 18:20.349
You found your brother?

18:20.432 --> 18:22.684
That's great, Asa-chan.

18:22.768 --> 18:24.228
Yuru-kun, right?

18:24.311 --> 18:28.732
I've heard about you from... Asa-chan...

18:29.316 --> 18:31.860
These are my brother's Daemons,
Right and Left.

18:31.944 --> 18:33.487
Nice to meet you.

18:34.404 --> 18:38.117
Sorry I couldn't help
when you were in trouble, Jin-kun.

18:38.200 --> 18:40.619
I crashed after my deadline.

18:40.702 --> 18:43.413
Not at all. Good work
meeting your deadline.

18:43.497 --> 18:45.040
This is bad.

18:45.124 --> 18:49.128
We had a barrier around the mansion
to keep outsiders away.

18:49.211 --> 18:51.630
It makes you wonder
when and how they got in.

18:52.297 --> 18:57.386
We'll tor—interrogate the ones
we captured again.

18:57.469 --> 18:59.054
Man, this sucks.

18:59.138 --> 19:02.015
The mansion isn't safe anymore.

19:02.099 --> 19:03.892
I won't be able to rest easily.

19:05.727 --> 19:07.146
That's Dad's car.

19:07.938 --> 19:10.149
The master has returned.

19:21.660 --> 19:23.203
Hello, sir.

19:23.287 --> 19:26.331
Hey. Sounds like you ran
into some trouble.

19:26.415 --> 19:29.459
Hello and good morning.

19:30.669 --> 19:32.004
Master, is that...?

19:32.629 --> 19:34.631
I'm Tadera Ryu.

19:34.715 --> 19:37.384
We ran into each other,
so I gave him a ride.

19:37.467 --> 19:38.886
He's from the Tadera clan.

19:38.969 --> 19:41.430
Apparently, he's Yuru-kun's guardian.

19:41.513 --> 19:43.182
Are you okay, Yuru?

19:43.265 --> 19:46.435
Ah, so you're Yuru-kun.

19:46.518 --> 19:48.353
I'm Kagemori Gonzo, head of the clan.

19:48.437 --> 19:49.938
Nice to meet you.

19:50.022 --> 19:51.857
I've heard about you two.

19:51.940 --> 19:54.151
Your Daemons sure are impressive.

19:55.152 --> 19:58.363
The Tadera clan,
retainers of Higashi Village.

19:58.447 --> 20:01.450
They serve as liaisons between
Higashi Village and the outside world.

20:01.533 --> 20:07.414
They're a cautious clan that's never
shown themselves to us before.

20:08.040 --> 20:12.085
So what's one of them doing defenseless
in the middle of enemy territory?

20:12.836 --> 20:15.923
Could the Kagemoris and Dera
be working together?

20:16.006 --> 20:16.840
No.

20:17.591 --> 20:22.095
I can feel that the old man and Jin
genuinely want to kill him.

20:22.888 --> 20:26.600
What did the Tadera clan
do to the Kagemoris?

20:27.184 --> 20:28.227
Dera-san.

20:28.310 --> 20:29.436
What's up?

20:29.519 --> 20:35.359
She told me that I'd acquire
the power of Seal if I die.

20:35.984 --> 20:37.486
You knew about that, didn't you?

20:38.320 --> 20:40.239
Right and Left,
why didn't you tell me either?

20:41.949 --> 20:44.284
I just heard the village legend.

20:44.368 --> 20:45.953
I don't know the details.

20:46.036 --> 20:49.831
But you're a kind and caring brother.

20:49.915 --> 20:52.167
If someone did something
to Asa-chan and blackmailed you,

20:52.251 --> 20:54.002
you'd throw your life away.

20:54.920 --> 20:57.339
Knowing you can die once

20:57.422 --> 21:00.926
and be fine makes it easier
to act recklessly.

21:01.009 --> 21:02.511
That's a dangerous way to think.

21:02.594 --> 21:06.640
There's no guarantee
you'll come back to life.

21:06.723 --> 21:12.646
Remember how we said you're the first
Higashi Village twins in 400 years?

21:13.313 --> 21:16.024
One of the last twins
didn't come back to life.

21:24.074 --> 21:27.619
Okay. This isn't a conversation
to have standing around.

21:28.203 --> 21:30.414
Yuru-kun, are you hungry?

21:30.497 --> 21:31.331
What?

21:31.832 --> 21:34.376
Come to think of it,
I haven't had anything since last night.

21:34.459 --> 21:38.463
Then let's talk over breakfast.

21:38.547 --> 21:39.381
Hey!

21:40.716 --> 21:43.010
Tell everyone to prepare breakfast!

21:43.093 --> 21:44.594
Yes, sir!

21:44.678 --> 21:47.139
Don't worry. I won't poison you.

21:48.890 --> 21:51.810
I appreciate that. Thanks for the meal.

21:52.728 --> 21:55.147
Breakfast with Brother!

23:27.531 --> 23:28.824
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:28.907 --> 23:32.077
I'm Hagure Hikaru. I'm a mangaka.

23:32.160 --> 23:34.329
What's a mangaka?

23:34.412 --> 23:37.833
Every time twins are born,
the world is thrown into chaos.

23:37.916 --> 23:40.836
Translator: Sho Stifler
